Paragraph 2 discusses Fair-Count-Min, an unbiased estimator of ng, and provides a probabilistic bound on estimation accuracy during steady-state phase initialization using exact counts from warm-up phase. It also addresses potential unfairness introduced by group size estimates and the dependency of fairness impacts on stream distribution. Additionally, it acknowledges susceptibility to compromise under adversarial conditions and mentions mitigation strategies requiring larger memory footprints in Section 8.3.

