The following data is given in a table format with two columns: "citation" and "context". The task is to create an algorithm that can be used for fairness-aware hashing, which means it should take into account both individual fairness (where each item gets assigned to its nearest neighbor) and group fairness. 

The existing work on fairness in data structures [11–13,78] is limited and only focuses on individual fairness in near-neighbor search. Shahbazi et al. have studied this topic but their approach does not consider the case where there are multiple items with similar features that should be treated equally.
